 "summary": {
  "text": "The story is the planned closure of the National Archives facility at San Bruno, cast as a threat to irreplaceable regional records. August 20 produced no posts, only a single member retweet; the first original post came August 24, describing the archives as holding \"stories, memories, and history,\" not \"boxes of paper.\" August 25 was again retweet-only. August 26 shifted from the records to community mobilization, thanking press conference attendees and pledging to continue. August 30 returned to preservation language, widening the frame from local to Bay Area, California and beyond. This is entirely @RepKevinMullin — three posts, one member, no co-signers — a single-district concern, not a caucus push. Open: whether anyone joins him, and whether the closure proceeds.",
